    "ar": "اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي عَبْدُكَ، وَابْنُ عَبْدِكَ، وَابْنُ أَمَتِكَ، نَاصِيَتِي بِيَدِكَ، مَاضٍ فِيَّ حُكْمُكَ، عَدْلٌ فِيَّ قَضَاؤُكَ، أَسْأَلُكَ بِكُلِّ اسْمٍ هُوَ لَكَ، سَمَّيْتَ بِهِ نَفْسَكَ، أَوْ أَنْزَلْتَهُ فِي كِتَابِكَ، أَوْ عَلَّمْتَهُ أَحَدًا مِنْ خَلْقِكَ، أَوِ اسْتَأْثَرْتَ بِهِ فِي عِلْمِ الْغَيْبِ عِنْدَكَ، أَنْ تَجْعَلَ الْقُرْآنَ رَبِيعَ قَلْبِي، وَنُورَ صَدْرِي، وَجَلَاءَ حُزْنِي، وَذَهَابَ هَمِّي",
    "lo": {
      "en": "Allahumma inni 'abduka, wabnu 'abdika, wabnu amatika, nasiyati biyadika, madin fiyya hukmuka, 'adlun fiyya qada'uka, as'aluka bikullis-min huwa laka sammayta bihi nafsaka, aw anzaltahu fi kitabika, aw 'allamtahu ahadan min khalqika, awis-ta'tharta bihi fi 'ilmil-ghaybi 'indaka, an taj'alal-Qur'ana rabi'a qalbi, wa nura sadri, wa jala'a huzni, wa dhahaba hammi",
      "hi": "Allahumma inni 'abduka, wabnu 'abdika, wabnu amatika, nasiyati biyadika, madin fiyya hukmuka, 'adlun fiyya qada'uka, as'aluka bikullis-min huwa laka sammayta bihi nafsaka, aw anzaltahu fi kitabika, aw 'allamtahu ahadan min khalqika, awis-ta'tharta bihi fi 'ilmil-ghaybi 'indaka, an taj'alal-Qur'ana rabi'a qalbi, wa nura sadri, wa jala'a huzni, wa dhahaba hammi",
      "ur": "Allahumma inni 'abduka, wabnu 'abdika, wabnu amatika, nasiyati biyadika, madin fiyya hukmuka, 'adlun fiyya qada'uka, as'aluka bikullis-min huwa laka sammayta bihi nafsaka, aw anzaltahu fi kitabika, aw 'allamtahu ahadan min khalqika, awis-ta'tharta bihi fi 'ilmil-ghaybi 'indaka, an taj'alal-Qur'ana rabi'a qalbi, wa nura sadri, wa jala'a huzni, wa dhahaba hammi"
    },
    "me": {
      "en": "O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or revealed in Your Book, or taught to any of Your creation, or preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the banisher of my grief, and the reliever of my anxiety.",
      "hi": "O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or revealed in Your Book, or taught to any of Your creation, or preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the banisher of my grief, and the reliever of my anxiety.",
      "ur": "O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or revealed in Your Book, or taught to any of Your creation, or preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the banisher of my grief, and the reliever of my anxiety."
    },
    "title": {
      "en": "For Removing Sorrow, Anxiety, and Depression",
      "hi": "चिंता, डिप्रेशन व उदासी दूर करने की दुआ",
      "ur": "चिंता, डिप्रेशन व उदासी दूर करने की दुआ"
    },
    "tm": {
      "en": "Whenever stricken with worry, sadness, anxiety, or depression.",
      "hi": "Whenever stricken with worry, sadness, anxiety, or depression.",
      "ur": "Whenever stricken with worry, sadness, anxiety, or depression."
    },
    "how": {
      "en": "The Prophet ﷺ instructed: 'Whoever is afflicted with grief should recite this and learn it.' Virtue & Benefit: The Prophet ﷺ guaranteed that Allah will replace his grief and anxiety with joy and relief.",
      "hi": "The Prophet ﷺ instructed: 'Whoever is afflicted with grief should recite this and learn it.' फ़ज़ीलत: The Prophet ﷺ guaranteed that Allah will replace his grief and anxiety with joy and relief.",
      "ur": "The Prophet ﷺ instructed: 'Whoever is afflicted with grief should recite this and learn it.' فضیلت: The Prophet ﷺ guaranteed that Allah will replace his grief and anxiety with joy and relief."
    },
    "ref": "Musnad Ahmad & Sahih Ibn Hibban (Musnad Ahmad 3712 / Ibn Hibban 972) | Sahih",
    "active": true
  },
  {
    "id": "dua_v_027",
    "cat": "protection",
    "subcat": "for_relief_from_anxiety,_",
    "allCats": [
